  "id": "COMPOUND:17179 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Lupinine and DNA polymerase iota, mediated through multiple intermediate targets. Lupinine is identified as a target of several compounds, including Macrophage scavenger receptor types I and II, which in turn are targets of various metabolites. These metabolites, such as Methyl (23R,25R)-3,4-Seco-9Beta-H-Lanosta-4(28),7-Dien-26,23-Olid-3-Oate and (1R,3R,10R,11R,14S)-14-hydroxy-3,7,12-trimethyl-2,9-dioxatetracyclo[9.3.0.01,3.06,10]tetradeca-6,12-dien-8-one, all have DNA polymerase iota as their target. This indicates a chain of interactions where Lupinine may influence DNA polymerase iota through these intermediates. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, suggesting a possible mechanism involving the modulation of macrophage scavenger receptors and their downstream effects on DNA polymerase iota. The strength of the evidence is supported by multiple high-scoring paths, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
